<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 85,656 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 85,656 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 85,656 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Saturday compared to 51,036 tonnes in the same period on Friday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Saturday    June 13</p>
<p>    Export cargo		26,848	 7,639</p>
<p>    Import cargo		58,808	43,397</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ship sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Jet A-1 fuel	 25,000	 Al-Badiyah		14/6</p>
<p>Palm oil	     10,000	 Wawasan Courage	 16/6</p>
<p>Sugar		  13,512	 Ruvu			16/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 Themera		   17/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		6,000	 Bunga Siantan	   22/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
